WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Who could encourage an apostle?

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.280
In Romans one,

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.420
Paul longs to visit the believers

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.080
in Rome and strengthen them.

5
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.520
Then he explains that they will be

6
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.780
mutually encouraged by each other’s faith,

7
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.600
both theirs and his.

8
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.360
Paul expects to receive encouragement too.

9
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.660
The faith of ordinary believers matters even

10
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.400
to an apostle.

11
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.940
This helps us see service as something

12
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:26.600
we share.

13
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.440
God brings people together who can strengthen

14
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.060
one another.

15
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.360
So when you speak with someone at

16
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.160
church this week,

17
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.220
ask how they are trusting Christ.

18
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.680
Listen for what their faith can teach

19
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.140
you.

20
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:39.800
Share honestly too.

21
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.780
Faithfulness includes giving encouragement and receiving it.

22
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.260
Your place in that conversation matters.
